Third-party notices
------------------------------------------------------------------------

This software is built on top of Polars (https://pola.rs/), licensed
under the MIT License.

CAFE imputation (the optional `cafe_impute` / `CafeImputer` components) is
powered by `cafe-impute`, developed at Sov.ai and licensed under the MIT
License. It is an optional dependency installed via the `cafe` extra.

The catch22 feature set, when implemented in Panelary, is a clean-room
reimplementation from the published description in:

    Lubba, C.H., Sethi, S.S., Knaute, P., Schultz, S.R., Fulcher, B.D.,
    & Jones, N.S. (2019). "catch22: CAnonical Time-series CHaracteristics."
    Data Mining and Knowledge Discovery, 33, 1821-1852.

Panelary does NOT vendor, copy, or link the GPL-licensed `pycatch22`
implementation. Any catch22 features shipped by Panelary are
independently implemented from the paper and licensed under Apache-2.0.

The QUANT (Dempster, Schmidt & Webb, 2023, arXiv:2308.00928), Hydra (Dempster,
Schmidt & Webb, 2023, Data Mining and Knowledge Discovery) and MiniRocket
(Dempster, Schmidt & Webb, 2021, KDD) transforms in `panelary.embed` are
clean-room reimplementations from the published descriptions. Panelary does NOT
vendor, copy, or link the GPL-3.0 reference implementations, and their
implementers did not read them or the aeon / sktime / wildboar ports. The causal
MiniRocket (`CausalMiniRocket`) also departs from the paper deliberately (causal
alignment, trailing pooling, row-subsample biases). All are licensed under
Apache-2.0.

